summary:
I read research/sf/lens-implications.md in full (613 lines) and checked about 540 claims against their sources. Those sources were the host at 81f1cd96 (every OBSERVED path:line was opened), all six system notes, FILE-M items 659-662, 683, 693, 694, 714, 737 and 749, PROGRESS J375-J384, FOLD §2, and V13 §8.5 H13-H30. 25 claims do not hold: 1 WRONG, 1 UNSUPPORTED and 23 IMPRECISE.

The WRONG one (L21): the note credits the rule that wild land stays wild to the owner (J377), but it is the session's vetoable reading recorded in J377. The UNSUPPORTED one (L1): the note calls the aggression chip public, but ALIGN says it is shown to the DM on Library/Realm cards and in the premium PDF, and no player-facing surface was traced.

Four findings (L10-L13) are readings of FILE-M that no longer match it. FILE-M has since been applied and then revised after J384, so the PENDING status, the quote "absent until the host bands its strength", the "raid won +1" verdict table and "criminal_network has no class" no longer match the file.

The rest are citation and precision fixes:
- line ranges and the §7.3 read list;
- the vassal rebellion that the cited lines do not show breaking a link;
- the subjugation threshold;
- the source of "no trade tie on contraband";
- H16's supposed "security term";
- embattlement entry without its weak-security condition;
- the stocks being "public" when that rests only on a designed veil;
- steadings "never on RRb" despite +S;
- a third door that applies RR (the World's Temper picker).

All 35 host asks rest on a host fact that their cited notes state and the code bears out. §6's 13 questions match J384's 13 answers one for one.

Not checkable without git: the map-module documents' line counts and read ranges as the note read them (the files have grown since), the pre-revision FILE-M text, and the uncommitted-edits state at commit 7d04e75.

